==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:unlykely|:afeq|un-<id:negative>|likely|:afeq|un-<id:negative>|like|-ly<id:adverbial>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|unlykely,unlikly,unlykly,unlicli}}. {{surf|en|un-<id:negative>|likely}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌnˈlaɪkli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-unlikely.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-GB-unlikely.ogg|a=UK}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er,more}}

# Not [[likely]]; improbable; not to be reasonably expected.
#: {{ux|en|It is pretty '''unlikely''' that you'll win, but I will pray that at least you [[do well]].}}
#: {{ux|en|In the highly '''unlikely''' event of landing in water, lifejackets are stored under the seat.}}
#* {{RQ:Wells Time Machine|chapter=X|text=Now, I still think that for this box of matches to have escaped the wear of time for immemorial years was a strange, and for me, a most fortunate thing. Yet oddly enough I found here a far more '''unlikely''' substance, and that was camphor.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Kevin Liptak|title=With stiff tariffs he promised now in place, Trump opens a new trade war|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/02/01/politics/tariffs-trump-campaign-promise|date=2025-02-01|passage=Saturday’s tariffs are '''unlikely''' to be Trump’s last. The president said himself said in the Oval Office that additional tariffs could come by mid-February on chips, pharmaceuticals, steel, aluminum, copper, oil and gas imports – along with tariffs on the European Union – all threats that few would discount given his willingness to follow through on the North American and China tariffs on Saturday.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251121094734/https://www.cnn.com/2025/02/01/politics/tariffs-trump-campaign-promise|archivedate=21 November 2025}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2025-02-19|author=Mike Lewis|title=Tragedy at Moorgate|journal=RAIL|issue=1029|page=59, about the {{w|Moorgate tube crash}}|text=Nor had the post mortem on Newson's body revealed any illness or other physical condition that might have prevented him from applying the brake, although after four days in the oven-like heat of the wreckage, the body was so badly decomposed as to make any reliable post mortem results '''unlikely'''.}} 
# Not holding out a prospect of success; likely to fail; unpromising.
#: {{ux|en|'''unlikely''' means}}

