===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something or somebody considered [[unlikely]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980|author=Robert K. Lindsay|title=Applications of artificial intelligence for organic chemistry
|passage=The molecular ion candidates are divided by the testing phase into three categories: rejects, '''unlikelies''', and probables. Differences between each candidate and the prominent peaks in the spectrum are computed.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=Laurie R. King|title=To Play the Fool
|passage="Here is my every possible phone number, plus a few '''unlikelies'''. And I've also put down the numbers of Karin and Wade, in case you've lost them. Karin can come anytime; Wade, up until six in the morning."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Jack Canfield; Mark Victor Hansen; Marci Shimoff|title=Chicken soup for the mother's soul 2|page=166
|passage=Then the most unlikely of '''unlikelies''' happened. We got another phone call. Another woman wanted to give us a baby—a boy, born just that morning. We walked into a hospital, and he was placed into my arms.}}

